# Keep secrets OUT of the image.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, so without this file `.env` is baked into
# every image layer -- credentials sitting inside an artefact that gets copied
# around, long after they are rotated. Compose already injects them correctly
# at runtime via `env_file: .env`, and config/settings.py reads them with
# os.getenv(), so the baked copy was never the path that mattered.
#
# NOTE: python-dotenv's load_dotenv() does not override variables that are
# already set, so runtime env_file values won this race anyway -- but only by
# the library's default. Excluding the file removes the ambiguity entirely.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The money ledger and its WAL live here and are volume-mounted at runtime
# (./data:/app/data). Baking them in shipped a stale racing.db plus a 13MB
# results cache in every build.
data/
logs/

# Build noise
.git/
.gitignore
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store
*.log
